# Implementation Plan: Strict Omnisend Email-Click Revenue Attribution

## 1. Executive Summary & Objective
The objective is to implement **strict Omnisend email-click revenue attribution** for the Hungry Hub website (`https://hubhungry.vercel.app`).

By default, ecommerce tracking often sends every placed order to analytics platforms. This implementation introduces an **Attribution Gatekeeper** ensuring that Omnisend receives order and revenue events **ONLY** when an order directly originated from a verified Omnisend email click within an active attribution window (default: 7 days).

---

## 2. Attribution Scenarios

| Scenario | Traffic Source | Internal Order (Supabase) | Omnisend Revenue Attribution |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Scenario A** | Omnisend Email Click | Recorded normally | **YES (Attributed)** |
| **Scenario B** | Google / Organic Search | Recorded normally | **NO (Zero Event Sent)** |
| **Scenario C** | Direct Visit (Typed URL) | Recorded normally | **NO (Zero Event Sent)** |
| **Scenario D** | Social Media / Referral | Recorded normally | **NO (Zero Event Sent)** |
| **Scenario E** | Expired Email Click (> 7 days) | Recorded normally | **NO (Zero Event Sent)** |

---

## 3. Omnisend Link Anatomy & Detection Criteria

When a customer clicks a link in an Omnisend campaign or automation email, Omnisend appends query parameters to the destination URL. A visit qualifies as an Omnisend email click if **either** of the following conditions is met:

1. **Explicit UTM Parameters**:
   * `utm_source=omnisend` **AND** `utm_medium=email`
2. **Omnisend Identifiers**:
   * Presence of `omnisendContactID`, `omnisendAttributionID`, `omnisendMessageID`, or `omnisendCampaignID`.

Any visit without these markers is classified as non-email traffic (Direct, Search, or Social).

---

## 4. Architecture & Data Flow

```
[Customer clicks Omnisend email]
           │
           ▼
[Lands on Website with URL Params] ──► Captured by Omnisend Attribution Hook
           │                            │
           │                            ▼
           │                     Stored in localStorage
           │                     - source: "omnisend_email"
           │                     - clickedAt: timestamp
           │                     - expiresAt: timestamp + 7 days
           │                     - campaign / message IDs
           ▼
[Customer Browses, Adds to Cart, Logs In] ──► Attribution persists in localStorage
           │                                 ──► Bound to Supabase User ID on login
           ▼
[Customer Completes Checkout]
           │
           ▼
[Internal Order Created in Supabase]
           │
           ▼
[Attribution Gatekeeper Check]
     ├── Valid Omnisend Attribution & Unexpired?
     │         ├── YES ──► Check Order Idempotency (Not sent yet?)
     │         │                ├── YES ──► Emit `trackOmnisendPlacedOrder`
     │         │                │           Mark order as sent
     │         │                │           Expire/consume attribution
     │         │                └── NO  ──► Skip (prevent duplicate)
     │         │
     │         └── NO  ──► DO NOTHING (No call to Omnisend)
```

